abstract: >-
  The Thiele Machine is an abstract model of computation with states, moves,
  a step, a price per move, and a reading into an ordered set. Its toll
  requires a positive charge when a move carries the reading somewhere not
  at or below its previous value. The monograph develops retained
  distinctions, merges or fresh states, observation windows, and the room
  needed to preserve recoverable histories. Permanence and noninterference
  are additional restrictions where stated. A two-counter example realizes
  an earned CHECK, COMMIT and CERTIFY chain. This edition pairs the reviewed
  545-page PDF with the matching repository snapshot, which contains the
  complete 3,728- and 3,735-instruction universal programs and companion
  simulation proofs. The work also treats threshold readings of growing
  records and the recursion theorem under its stated representation
  assumptions. The RFC 9162 discussion concerns a specified protocol
  fragment; its conclusions depend on the observer model. The cost-framework
  comparisons are correspondences under stated premises, not full embeddings.
  Physical interpretations require their stated physical premises; the
  physical interpretation remains a thesis, and the pointer criterion is a thesis.
  No surveyed external consequence satisfied all four novelty and applicability criteria.
  The software is licensed Apache-2.0. The monograph and documentation are
  licensed CC-BY-SA-4.0.
